' Posting lifecycle overview; 12 named states summarize computed eligibility, persisted matching/analysis, and user review actions.
@startuml
title Posting lifecycle (12 states)
hide empty description

state Fetched
state "Merged as duplicate" as Merged
state "Filtered out" as Filtered
state Embedded
state Ranked
state Queued
state Analysed
state Reviewed
state Apply
state Skip
state Later
state "Expired / inactive" as Expired

[*] --> Fetched : validated source result
Fetched --> Merged : normalized company + title already exists
Fetched --> Filtered : active but fails title / location filters
Fetched --> Embedded : active + passes filters; cached vector or embed succeeds
Merged --> Embedded : canonical row passes filters and has / gets vector
Merged --> Filtered : canonical row is active but fails filters
Embedded --> Ranked : best compatible profile-section cosine score
Ranked --> Queued : percentile >= 97 AND similarity >= 0.55
Queued --> Analysed : valid JSON + verbatim evidence; cache by model
Analysed --> Reviewed : user submits valid action
Queued --> Reviewed : user reviews before analysis
Reviewed --> Apply : action = apply
Reviewed --> Skip : action = skip + allowed reason
Reviewed --> Later : action = later
Later --> Queued : remains queued; shown after unreviewed jobs
Queued --> Expired : next match detects inactivity and clears queue flag

legend bottom
  Logical stages, not a stored status column.
  Inactivity applies at any processing stage: deadline <= now;
  otherwise posted_at / first_seen falls outside the last 30 days.
  Filtered / unqueued rows remain stored for later matching.
  Failed embedding / analysis can retry on a later run.
  Reviews remain stored after expiry; Apply appears in Applied.
endlegend
@enduml
